{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["To begin — as written above: היום הזה אחל תת פחדך. The הַחִלּוֹתָ — the chet with a patach, and likewise הֶעֱרֹתִי מִצָּפוֹן, and likewise: הֶעֱדֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם. The form הַחִתּוֹת — like כִּיּוֹם מִדְיָן. But when the letters alef-chet-heh are not present, it says הֲרִיסוֹת, הֲקִימוֹת, הֲטִיבוֹת — all of them with a hatef. And I implored — in the midrash of parashat Shelach: 'Do not challenge him at the time of his vow.' From where? From Moshe: when he said to Israel: שִׁמְעוּ נָא הַמֹּרִים — the Holy One, blessed be He, swore that he would not enter the land, as it says: לָכֵן לֹא תָבִיאוּ וגו׳. Moshe said: It is a time of anger and a time of oath; I am not speaking now. He waited a year, and after that began to implore Him, as it says: וָאֶתְחַנַּן אֶל יהוה. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: Because you waited — the rest of the dead descend to Sheol but you shall ascend, as it says: עֲלֵה רֹאשׁ הַפִּסְגָּה וְתִרְאֶה מִשָּׁם."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The letters אחע״ה refer to the guttural letters alef, chet, ayin, heh that trigger patach in the definite article prefix; 'hatef' refers to hatef vowels that appear when these guttural letters are absent. The phrase 'hachitut kiyom midian' cites a form from another verse to illustrate the same phonological pattern."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:57.918125255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}